    {
      "id": "mg0ihu6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Part XIV-A was added to the Constitution by the 42nd Amendment Act, 1976, introducing Articles 323A and 323B.",
        "Article 323A enables Parliament to establish administrative tribunals exclusively for public service matters.",
        "Article 323B empowers Parliament and State Legislatures to establish tribunals for other specific matters such as taxation, foreign exchange, labor, and land reforms.",
        "Key quasi-judicial bodies in India include the Central Administrative Tribunal (CAT), State Administrative Tribunals (SAT), National Green Tribunal (NGT), and National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT)."
      ],
      "id": "g2jfgwa"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Service Matters",
          "value": "Article 323A",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Other Matters",
          "value": "Article 323B",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Added By",
          "value": "42nd Amendment",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Case",
          "value": "L. Chandra Kumar",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "4v6qfai"
    },
    {
      "id": "eix872k",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>INTRODUCTION</strong>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k16fnrj",
      "content": "Tribunals are quasi-judicial bodies established to deal with specific types of disputes. They were created to reduce the burden on regular courts and to provide speedy justice in specialized matters."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sgok8ga",
      "content": "Tribunals perform judicial as well as administrative functions and work under the supervision of the judiciary."
    },
    {
      "id": "ujctvsp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONSTITUTIONAL PROVISIONS RELATED TO TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lt3upwt",
      "content": "Tribunals were added to the Constitution by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976. They are mentioned in:"
    },
    {
      "id": "rbc2gvv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Article 323A – Administrative Tribunals</li><li>Article 323B – Other Tribunals</li></ul>",
        "Article 323A – Administrative Tribunals",
        "Article 323B – Other Tribunals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "96em6l2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ARTICLE 323A – ADMINISTRATIVE TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hhwfjk3",
      "content": "Article 323A empowers Parliament to establish Administrative Tribunals for:"
    },
    {
      "id": "m0zx9ur",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Service matters of central government employees</li><li>Disputes relating to recruitment and service conditions</li></ul>",
        "Service matters of central government employees",
        "Disputes relating to recruitment and service conditions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "71au7zs",
      "content": "Under this article, the Central Administrative Tribunal (CAT) was established in 1985."
    },
    {
      "id": "6pu704q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CENTRAL ADMINISTRATIVE TRIBUNAL (CAT)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w8o7yge",
      "content": "The CAT deals with service matters of:"
    },
    {
      "id": "nhwle65",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Central Government employees</li><li>Employees of Union Territories</li><li>Employees of public sector undertakings</li></ul>",
        "Central Government employees",
        "Employees of Union Territories",
        "Employees of public sector undertakings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b6djkp8",
      "content": "Features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "w5dldqu",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Headed by a Chairman</li><li>Benches across India</li><li>Decisions are subject to judicial review by High Court</li></ul>",
        "Headed by a Chairman",
        "Benches across India",
        "Decisions are subject to judicial review by High Court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "j06xc6l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "STATE ADMINISTRATIVE TRIBUNALS (SAT)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ljys8xd",
      "content": "State Governments can establish State Administrative Tribunals for their employees. Features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "cejarp6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Created with approval of Parliament</li><li>Can be abolished later</li><li>Decisions are appealable in High Court</li></ul>",
        "Created with approval of Parliament",
        "Can be abolished later",
        "Decisions are appealable in High Court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ljospr3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ARTICLE 323B – OTHER TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xdc8o0y",
      "content": "Article 323B allows establishment of tribunals for matters like:"
    },
    {
      "id": "0iizz55",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Taxation</li><li>Industrial disputes</li><li>Land reforms</li><li>Ceiling on urban property</li><li>Elections</li><li>Food procurement</li></ul>",
        "Taxation",
        "Industrial disputes",
        "Land reforms",
        "Ceiling on urban property",
        "Elections",
        "Food procurement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9ise76g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF TRIBUNALS UNDER ARTICLE 323B"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8v608fy",
      "content": "Important Tribunals include:"
    },
    {
      "id": "d8kygl2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Income Tax Appellate Tribunal (ITAT)</li><li>National Green Tribunal (NGT)</li><li>National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT)</li><li>National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission</li><li>Armed Forces Tribunal</li></ul>",
        "Income Tax Appellate Tribunal (ITAT)",
        "National Green Tribunal (NGT)",
        "National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT)",
        "National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission",
        "Armed Forces Tribunal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8rhmu28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NATIONAL GREEN TRIBUNAL (NGT)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pye16yu",
      "content": "Established in 2010 under NGT Act. Functions:"
    },
    {
      "id": "dam7krr",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Environmental protection</li><li>Forest conservation</li><li>Pollution control</li><li>Compensation for environmental damage</li></ul>",
        "Environmental protection",
        "Forest conservation",
        "Pollution control",
        "Compensation for environmental damage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11xy1dp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NATIONAL COMPANY LAW TRIBUNAL (NCLT)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nf9wmzw",
      "content": "NCLT deals with:"
    },
    {
      "id": "17506u4",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Company disputes</li><li>Insolvency cases</li><li>Corporate governance issues</li></ul>",
        "Company disputes",
        "Insolvency cases",
        "Corporate governance issues"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kzi9lcc",
      "content": "It replaced:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5td66dv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Company Law Board</li><li>BIFR</li><li>High Court jurisdiction in company matters</li></ul>",
        "Company Law Board",
        "BIFR",
        "High Court jurisdiction in company matters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9ecy6sx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ADVANTAGES OF TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "id": "kn7ar6u",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Speedy justice</li><li>Expert knowledge</li><li>Reduced burden on courts</li><li>Cost-effective</li><li>Simple procedures</li></ul>",
        "Speedy justice",
        "Expert knowledge",
        "Reduced burden on courts",
        "Cost-effective",
        "Simple procedures"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "54dd3aq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DISADVANTAGES OF TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "id": "o1mfbss",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Lack of judicial independence</li><li>Executive interference</li><li>Delay in appointments</li><li>Overlapping jurisdiction</li></ul>",
        "Lack of judicial independence",
        "Executive interference",
        "Delay in appointments",
        "Overlapping jurisdiction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ence0id",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TRIBUNALS VS COURTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Article 323A",
        "Article 323B"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Scope",
