          "Both Parliament and State Legislatures"
        ],
        [
          "Hierarchy",
          "No provision for hierarchy of tribunals",
          "A hierarchy of tribunals may be created"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "tovlkzn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vqexq7k",
      "content": "Tribunals:"
    },
    {
      "id": "r3xy0qu",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Specialized bodies</li><li>Flexible procedure</li><li>Technical expertise</li></ul>",
        "Specialized bodies",
        "Flexible procedure",
        "Technical expertise"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u9fuuwo",
      "content": "Courts:"
    },
    {
      "id": "8hz7agh",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Regular judicial bodies</li><li>Follow strict procedure</li><li>Deal with all types of cases</li></ul>",
        "Regular judicial bodies",
        "Follow strict procedure",
        "Deal with all types of cases"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hcfso7j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "JUDICIAL REVIEW OF TRIBUNALS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mf1dftm",
      "content": "Earlier, tribunal decisions were final. But after L. Chandra Kumar Case (1997):"
    },
    {
      "id": "u0lse18",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Judicial review by High Court and Supreme Court restored</li><li>Tribunals are subject to constitutional courts</li></ul>",
        "Judicial review by High Court and Supreme Court restored",
        "Tribunals are subject to constitutional courts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jrf0uqv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "IMPORTANT SUPREME COURT CASES"
    },
    {
      "id": "t58ftaa",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>L. Chandra Kumar Case (1997)</li><li>R. Gandhi Case</li><li>Madras Bar Association Case</li></ul>",
        "L. Chandra Kumar Case (1997)",
        "R. Gandhi Case",
        "Madras Bar Association Case"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2kkwsi5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TRIBUNALS REFORMS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3tt3ss",
      "content": "Reforms needed:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5chjpkf",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Uniform service conditions</li><li>Independent appointments</li><li>Reduction in executive control</li><li>Proper infrastructure</li></ul>",
        "Uniform service conditions",
        "Independent appointments",
        "Reduction in executive control",
        "Proper infrastructure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9r42f11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ROLE OF TRIBUNALS IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x66phdu",
      "content": "Tribunals play a vital role in:"
    },
    {
      "id": "6g4nm21",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Speedy justice delivery</li><li>Reducing pendency of courts</li><li>Specialized dispute resolution</li></ul>",
        "Speedy justice delivery",
        "Reducing pendency of courts",
        "Specialized dispute resolution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "oomnf0j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TRIBUNALS AND CONSTITUTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fzekocd",
      "content": "Tribunals must function within:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 323A tribunals can be established ONLY by Parliament, whereas Article 323B tribunals can be established by both Parliament and State Legislatures.",
        "In the landmark L. Chandra Kumar case (1997), the Supreme Court held that decisions of tribunals are subject to judicial review by High Courts.",
        "Tribunals are guided by the principles of natural justice and are not strictly bound by the procedure laid down in the Code of Civil Procedure (CPC)."
      ],
      "id": "tmp0x0m"
    },
    {
      "id": "irslhyy",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Constitutional limits</li><li>Principles of natural justice</li><li>Judicial review of higher courts</li></ul>",
        "Constitutional limits",
        "Principles of natural justice",
        "Judicial review of higher courts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vix7yr0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RECENT DEVELOPMENTS"
    },
    {
      "id": "s0urzy3",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Tribunal Reforms Act, 2021</li><li>Reduction in number of tribunals</li><li>Uniform tenure of members</li></ul>",
        "Tribunal Reforms Act, 2021",
        "Reduction in number of tribunals",
        "Uniform tenure of members"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "o2b60pv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM IMPORTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ihs76jk",
      "content": "Tribunals are important for:"
    },
    {
      "id": "b25f9nb",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>UPSC Prelims &amp; Mains</li><li>State PCS</li><li>Judiciary exams</li></ul>",
        "UPSC Prelims &amp; Mains",
        "State PCS",
        "Judiciary exams"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v6oy32n",
      "content": "Questions often asked from:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5yqun7i",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Articles 323A &amp; 323B</li><li>CAT &amp; NGT</li><li>Tribunal reforms</li></ul>",
        "Articles 323A &amp; 323B",
        "CAT &amp; NGT",
        "Tribunal reforms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "apw1ta3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONCLUSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g5xxuwi",
      "content": "Tribunals are an essential part of the Indian judicial system. They provide speedy and expert justice in specialized matters."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "myl9z36",
      "content": "However, proper reforms and independence are necessary to ensure their effective functioning."
    }
  ],
